<section class="section tech" id="cutti" aria-labelledby="shop-cutti-title">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="head " data-reveal><p class="kicker">CuTTI · private beta</p><h2 id="shop-cutti-title">Studio Tools, <em>Early Access</em>.</h2><p class="lead">CuTTI Studio and CuTTI Score are in private beta. A small number of composers, arrangers, engravers and music teachers can join now, at a special beta price that stays fixed for the whole beta period.</p></div>
<div class="grid grid--2">
  <article class="feature" data-reveal><h3>CuTTI Studio</h3><p>An idea generator and assistant arranger that builds sessions in the DAW. Describe a song in plain words, or give it a score, and CuTTI Studio plans the song and builds a ready-to-work session in Logic Pro, Cubase, Nuendo or Digital Performer.</p><span class="feature__tag">Private beta · special price</span></article>
  <article class="feature" data-reveal><h3>CuTTI Score</h3><p>A desktop app that turns printed music into scores to edit, play and use: from PDFs, scans and phone photos, and from recordings too.</p><span class="feature__tag">Private beta · special price</span></article>
</div>
<div class="beta" data-mt="40">
  <div data-reveal><p class="kicker">How it works</p><ol class="principles" data-mt="18"><li>Request access: say which tool you want, what you make, and which DAW or notation software you use.</li><li>You receive a personal access code and the beta price by email, usually within a few days.</li><li>Use the tools on your own work. Report what helps and what breaks; that feedback shapes the release.</li></ol></div>
  <div data-reveal><p class="kicker">The beta price</p><p class="lead" data-mt="18">The beta price is sent with your access code. It is lower than the price at release, and it does not change while the beta runs.</p><div class="btn-row" data-mt="24"><a class="btn btn--violet" href="/contact/?topic=cutti-beta">Request beta access</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/innovations/">About the tools</a></div><p class="small muted" data-mt="22">Beta means the tools are still changing: features will move, some things will break, and support is by email from the composer himself. Access codes are personal and not for sharing. CuTTI Studio runs on the Mac, with Logic Pro, Cubase, Nuendo or Digital Performer; CuTTI Score is a desktop app.</p></div>
</div>
